      "id": "spawn-node-b80d41",
      "name": "SpawnNode",
      "category": "BlueprintNodeSpawner",
      "signature": "SpawnNode<NodeType>(Target, Parent Graph, Bindings, Location, Post Spawn Delegate)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "UBlueprintNodeSpawner*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Parent Graph",
          "type": "UEdGraph*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Bindings",
          "type": "FBindingSet&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Location",
          "type": "FVector2D"
        },
        {
          "name": "Post Spawn Delegate",
          "type": "FCustomizeNodeDelegate"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<class NodeType> NodeType*",
      "docs": "Simplified version of the other SpawnNode(), that just let's sub-classes\nspecify their own post-spawn delegate (the node class is comes directly\nfrom the template parameter).\n@param  ParentGraph\t\t\tThe graph you want the node spawned into.\n@param  Bindings\t\t\t\tThe bindings to apply to the node (post spawn).\n@param  Location\t\t\t\tWhere you want the new node positioned in the graph.\n@param  PostSpawnDelegate\tA delegate to run after spawning the node, but prior to allocating the node's pins.\n@return Null if it failed to spawn a node (if NodeClass is null), otherwise a newly spawned node."
    },
